The function `groupBy` will take an array `arr` and a function `keyFn` as arguments. It will iterate over the array, applying the `keyFn` to each element to determine the key under which the element should be grouped. The result will be an object where each key maps to an array of elements that share that key, preserving the order of elements as they appeared in the input array. Edge cases include handling arrays with duplicate keys, empty arrays, and ensuring that the function works correctly with non-string keys.

ANSWER:
```javascript
function groupBy(arr, keyFn) {
  const result = {};
  arr.forEach(item => {
    const key = keyFn(item);
    if (!result[key]) {
      result[key] = [];
    }
    result[key].push(item);
  });
  return result;
}

module.exports = groupBy;
```

