The function `zip(a, b)` will take two arrays as input and return a new array where each element is a two-element array consisting of corresponding elements from the input arrays. The function will stop pairing elements once the end of the shorter array is reached, ensuring that no out-of-bounds errors occur. Edge cases include when one or both arrays are empty, in which case the function should return an empty array.

ANSWER:
```javascript
function zip(a, b) {
  const result = [];
  const minLength = Math.min(a.length, b.length);
  for (let i = 0; i < minLength; i++) {
    result.push([a[i], b[i]]);
  }
  return result;
}

module.exports = zip;
```

