The function `zip` will take two arrays of types `A[]` and `B[]` as input and return an array of tuples `[A, B][]`. The length of the returned array will be determined by the shorter of the two input arrays, ensuring that no out-of-bounds errors occur during the zipping process. Edge cases include when one or both arrays are empty, in which case the function should return an empty array.

ANSWER:
```typescript
function zip<A, B>(a: A[], b: B[]): [A, B][] {
  const minLength = Math.min(a.length, b.length);
  const result: [A, B][] = [];

  for (let i = 0; i < minLength; i++) {
    result.push([a[i], b[i]]);
  }

  return result;
}
```

