The function `partition` will take an array `arr` of type `T[]` and a predicate function `pred` that takes an element of type `T` and returns a boolean. The function will return a tuple containing two arrays: the first array will contain all elements from `arr` for which `pred` returns true, and the second array will contain all elements for which `pred` returns false. This implementation ensures that the function works correctly even with empty arrays or predicates that always return the same value.

ANSWER:
```typescript
export function partition<T>(arr: T[], pred: (t: T) => boolean): [T[], T[]] {
  const truthy: T[] = [];
  const falsy: T[] = [];

  for (const item of arr) {
    if (pred(item)) {
      truthy.push(item);
    } else {
      falsy.push(item);
    }
  }

  return [truthy, falsy];
}
```

