To create a TypeScript function that returns an array of unique elements while preserving the original order, we can utilize a `Set` to track elements that have already been encountered. This approach ensures that each element is added to the result array only once, maintaining the order in which they first appear. An edge case to consider is when the input array contains objects or arrays, as strict equality (`===`) will not work correctly for these types. To handle such cases, we can use a custom comparison function or convert objects to strings for comparison purposes.

